    }
  ],
  "prose": [
    {
      "text": "\"Which connectors serve this application, and why does traffic fail?\" needs the server group questions answered in order."
    },
    {
      "steps": [
        {
          "label": "What is a server group, and what selects it?",
          "text": "The segment names it, and a policy rule can override it: [[zpa.server-groups.role]]."
        },
        {
          "label": "Does it hold servers or discover them?",
          "text": "Dynamic Server Discovery against explicit servers, and the defaults that differ between sources: [[zpa.server-groups.discovery-mode]]."
        },
        {
          "label": "Which App Connector groups does it bind?",
          "text": "The connector list, how a connector is picked, and what is not known about an empty list: [[zpa.server-groups.connector-binding]]."
        },
        {
          "label": "Is there more than one server group on the segment?",
          "text": "Weights, passive flags and the Multimatch rules: [[zpa.server-groups.multiple-on-segment]]."
        },
        {
          "label": "Is the chain from segment to connected connector intact?",
          "text": "The hop-by-hop check: [[zpa.server-groups.chain-check]]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Python SDK's update body is in [[zpa.server-groups.update-payload]]. The Terraform delete cleanup is in [[zpa.server-groups.delete]] and, for failure handling shared with other objects, in [[zpa.terraform.delete-paths]]."
    },
    {
      "text": "Policy rules that scope on segment groups, rather than on server groups, are covered in [[zpa.segment-groups.policy-use]] and [[zpa.policy.criteria]]. The segments that carry server groups are in [[zpa.app-segments]]. The App Connector side is in [[zpa.app-connectors.connector-groups]]."
    },
    {
      "text": "{{inconsistent-config-details-contract}}"
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither SDK model carries the field: [[zpa.api.server-groups-wire:inconsistent-config-details-sdk-models]]."
    }
  ],
